AOWIS Server Map for Debian
===========================

The package creates and starts aowis-server-map.service on first installation.
Its configuration is stored at:

  /etc/aowis-server-map/map-server.ini

The package generates separate read and delete API keys when this file does not
already exist. Existing configuration is preserved during upgrades and ordinary
package removal. It is deleted only when the package is purged.

Apache reverse-proxy templates are installed directly as disabled sites:

  /etc/apache2/sites-available/aowis-map.localhost.conf
  /etc/apache2/sites-available/aowis-server-map.conf

Edit and enable exactly one template. For example:

  sudoedit /etc/apache2/sites-available/aowis-map.localhost.conf
  sudo a2ensite aowis-map.localhost.conf
  sudo apache2ctl configtest
  sudo systemctl reload apache2

The Internet-facing template contains placeholder domain and origin values and
must be edited before it is enabled. It is intended to be completed with:

  sudo certbot --apache --redirect -d maps.example.com

Service administration:

  sudo systemctl status aowis-server-map.service
  sudo journalctl -u aowis-server-map.service -f
  sudo systemctl restart aowis-server-map.service
